# Ansel's log, in the wreck's cabin.
dialogue log
  node open narrator "My father's log. His writing leans forward, like he did. Three years ago the cargo and the weather stop. Then something else starts."
    -> trick
  node trick narrator "“Yellow flag at the reef mouth. Fog out of a clear sky. It smells of kelp. Boats came alongside. QUARANTINE, they said. They had forms.”"
    -> reef
  node reef narrator "“Ran for the Needle without the compass. Brave. Then I put her on the reef. They took the lads off anyway. Salt camp. Gullet Key.”"
    -> rows
  node rows narrator "After that the entries get short. A ship's name. A crew. A flag number. Six ships. Fifteen flags. Then the last page, in bright ink."
    -> stop
  node stop narrator "I read the first line. I don't read the second. The words stay where they are. So do I."
    > "(Hold the log out to Quill.)" -> reads
    > "It's the light in here. It's a wreck." -> salt
  node salt narrator "“It's a wreck,” Quill says. She takes the log out of my hands. “Budge up.”"
    -> reads
  node reads quill "(reading) “Lise, number fifteen is the blue one. Our boy will have the compass by now. If I'm late, he'll know what to do with it.”"
    -> anyway
  node anyway quill "“He won't. He'll do it anyway.”"
    -> lise
  node lise narrator "Lise. The L on the flag. Fifteen flags, sewn out of shirts. Every one signed for her."
    -> mother
  node mother quill "…Your mother."
    -> idiot
  node idiot quill "Your father's an idiot."
    -> warmly
  node warmly quill "I mean that nicely."
    > "Thank you for reading it." -> thanks
      add aff 1
    > "He's spelled “quarantine” wrong. Twice." -> spelling
  node thanks quill "You'd have got there. I just got there first. Don't make me do it twice."
  node spelling quill "You're proofreading your father. Now? …Show me. Oh, that's terrible. Idiot."
    -> fond
  node fond narrator "She says it the same way as before. Warmly."
